0Fortement inspiré de  l'article disponible sur https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Ivan-Zmitrovich/publication/270882938_A_Survey_of_Species_of_Genus_Trametes_Fr_Higher_Basidiomycetes_with_Estimation_of_Their_Medicinal_Source_Potential/links/00b7d534e4a04b86d8000000/A-Survey-of-Species-of-Genus-Trametes-Fr-Higher-Basidiomycetes-with-Estimation-of-Their-Medicinal-Source-Potential.pdf///examen micro : A microscopical study of basidiomata was carried out as described by Gilbertson and Ryvarden. Freehand sections and squash mounts of basidiomata were examined in 5% KOH and 2% Cotton Blue. Spore conglomerations in Trametes are more easily detected in basidiocarps’ upper surface06071727221500
